  "name": "Question 15",
  "problem": "Find the derivative of $y={e}^{x}sec\u2061(x).$\n\n$\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}={e}^{x}sec\u2061(x)($\n{{field-1}}\n$)$",
  "worked_solution": "We calculate the derivative using the product rule, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}\\,({e}^{x}sec\u2061(x)) \\\\  & ={e}^{x}sec\u2061(x)+{e}^{x}sec\u2061(x)tan\u2061(x) \\\\  & ={e}^{x}sec\u2061(x)(1+tan\u2061(x))\\end{aligned}\n$$",
